---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Soha Sami"
  description="About Soha Sami, her academic background, research interests and Erasmus Mundus journey."
  active="about"
>

  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT</p>
    <h1>About me</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="section-wrap">
    <div class="prose">

      <p>
        I&rsquo;m Soha, a graduate student in energy markets, quantitative finance and climate risk.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am currently completing the
        <strong>Erasmus Mundus GrEnFin programme in Greening Energy Market and Finance</strong>,
        a triple-degree programme that has taken me to
        <strong>Università di Bologna, LMU Munich and Université Paris Dauphine-PSL</strong>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Moving between Italy, Germany and France has been an important part of the programme.
        I have experienced three different academic environments and had the chance to see how
        energy, finance and climate-related questions are approached from different perspectives.
      </p>

      <h2>Education</h2>

      <h3>Erasmus Mundus GrEnFin</h3>

      <p class="meta">
        <strong>Greening Energy Market and Finance &middot; 2025&ndash;2027</strong>
      </p>

      <h4>Bologna &middot; Università di Bologna</h4>

      <p>
        Bologna was the first stage of my GrEnFin programme. My studies there introduced me
        to European energy markets and the economic and financial questions surrounding them.
      </p>

      <h4>Munich &middot; LMU Munich</h4>

      <p>
        Munich was the second stage of my GrEnFin programme, where I continued developing
        my understanding of quantitative methods.
      </p>

      <h4>Paris &middot; Université Paris Dauphine-PSL</h4>

      <p>
        I am currently in <strong>Paris</strong>, studying at Université Paris Dauphine-PSL.
        Here, my GrEnFin studies include <strong>Climate &amp; Business</strong>, giving me
        a different perspective on climate-related questions, business and the changing
        role of finance.
      </p>

      <h3>BA Economics &amp; Mathematics</h3>

      <p class="meta">
        <strong>University of Delhi &middot; 2021&ndash;2025</strong>
      </p>

      <p>
        Before moving to Europe, I studied Economics and Mathematics at the University of
        Delhi in New Delhi. This gave me the foundation in economics, mathematics, statistics
        and quantitative analysis that I have carried into my graduate studies.
      </p>

      <h2>From New Delhi to Bologna, Munich and Paris</h2>

      <p>
        I started my academic life in <strong>New Delhi</strong> and then moved to Europe
        for GrEnFin. Since then, I have lived and studied in
        <strong>Bologna, Munich and Paris</strong>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Living in three countries has also given me a closer view of the European energy and
        finance landscape. The questions may be shared across Europe, but the way they are
        discussed and studied can differ significantly between countries. That perspective
        has become an important part of how I approach my own research.
      </p>

      <p>
        The <strong>Erasmus Mundus scholarship</strong> is what made this path possible.
        It has allowed me to study in different countries and universities while building
        a broader understanding of the field I want to work in.
      </p>

      <h2>What I study</h2>

      <p>
        My interests are centred on <strong>energy markets, climate risk and quantitative
        methods</strong>. I am particularly interested in electricity markets, market design,
        renewable generation, flexibility, power prices, uncertainty and risk.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am also developing my quantitative and computational skills through stochastic
        modelling, numerical methods, statistics, Python and research.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
